Package: rtfqc
Title: Read Clinical RTF Outputs and Check Them Against QC Data
Version: 0.1.14
Authors@R:
    person("Xianhua", "Zeng", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "huazizeng@gmail.com")
Description: Reads RTF (Rich Text Format) tables, listings and figures
    produced for clinical study reports (for example by 'SAS' ODS RTF or
    'r2rtf') directly, without 'Word', 'LibreOffice' or 'Pandoc'. Splits them into pages with titles,
    headers, table body and footnotes, rebuilds the body table as a data
    frame, and compares it cell by cell with an independently programmed
    QC dataset, classifying each difference as a value difference,
    truncation, rounding, number format or spacing. Also checks
    "Page x of y" numbering, blank pages, and titles and footnotes
    against a table of contents. Works on single files or whole folders.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    utils
